<title>UK: UK net consumer credit up 853 mln stg in January.</title>
<headline>UK net consumer credit up 853 mln stg in January.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following seasonally adjusted consumer credit data -</p>
<p>NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN STG)</p>
<p>					     Jan     Dec 96	   Jan,96</p>
<p> Total net lending		     2,767   2,664 (2,625)  2,033</p>
<p>  -- Consumer credit		     853     983 (1,022)    664</p>
<p>  -- Secured on dwellings	    1,914   1,681  (1,603) 1,368</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN of net consumer lending BY SOURCE -</p>
<p>  -- Banks				 631   444	(459)   550</p>
<p>  -- Building societies		 28    31	 (33)    29</p>
<p>  -- Other specialist lenders	188   501	(525)    96</p>
<p>  -- Retailers			    10    10	  (8)   -10</p>
<p>  -- Insurance companies		-4    -3	 (-3)    -1</p>
<p> Credit card				88   141	(184)    226</p>
<p>NOTE - forecast 900 million stg rise in new consumer credit  </p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted, in PCT)</p>
<p>					     Jan    Dec 96</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	     1.2     1.3</p>
<p>		3 mth annualised	16.9    17.0</p>
<p>		year-on-year	    16.7    16.6</p>
<p> Total personal borrowing mth/mth  0.6     0.6</p>
<p>			3mth annualised  7.2     7.4</p>
<p>				  yr/yr    6.7     6.6</p>
<p> Secured on dwellings mth/mth	0.5     0.4</p>
<p>			3mth annualised  5.5     5.8</p>
<p>		     yr/yr		 5.0     4.9</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
